The first triage result is important: the prior “enumerate every pairwise distance” verifier is not viable. The paper’s code contains \(q^{2n}\) matrices, so enumeration is exponential in the field size, while a submitted witness must remain short. The promising native family is instead Section 4’s equivalence criterion: inverse-generate two members known to be equivalent and ask for the explicit semilinear/congruence witness. That keeps the paper’s finite-field/code objects and permits exact substitution-based checking; I’m now checking whether its exponent equation is genuinely hard or collapses to routine root extraction.
