The prototype now builds and verifies the native \(8\times8\) symmetric code instances. The key algebra checks out: every planted coefficient vector annihilates the supplied plane and its matrix has exact rank 6; independent elimination recovers the same projective witness in roughly 2,600–4,000 counted operations, versus the 40-operation structural bound. I’m moving through the full gate suite now, with special attention to corruption reasons, relabelling invariance, and whether any cheap coefficient ansatz accidentally hits the one-dimensional solution line.
