codex
The preserved \(88\times88\) version passes every local gate, but the audit found two claims that must be corrected before it is trustworthy: the measured reference cost is about 93,000 operations (not “more than one million”), and the stored `eta = -1` is not a nonsquare in the even extension \(\mathbb F_{p^8}\). The latter does not affect the constructed word because \(b_2=0\), so \(\eta\) never appears; I’m removing that misleading metadata and stating the correct existential choice of any extension-field nonsquare. I’m also making the non-demo ladder grow only the field size at fixed 176-atom answer shape.
codex
All mandatory local gates pass. The measured Track B gap is 92,680 modular scalar operations on average for exact RREF versus 203 operations for the intended transport route; the reference algorithm solves 8/8 as expected, while all five no-tool attacks solve 0/8. The structure-aware guess test found 0 valid answers in 200,000 samples, and the demo has exactly 48 ordered kernel bases. I’ve corrected the profile to those measurements and am moving to the script-owned four-vendor hardening run.
